<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    Diagnostics behaviour checks — the controlled-exception test for the
    failure-only log (round 33).

    Follows the repository's established verification convention
    (Theme/step1.d.tests, step2.f.ClientTests, step3.f.UserTests,
    step4.f.CompanyTests): a Windows console executable that references the
    application and asserts behaviour, exiting nonzero on failure. No
    test-framework package is introduced.

    Scope: an isolated folder through AppDataRoot.TestFolderOverride — the real
    %APPDATA%\ProGlassAutomation folder is never touched and the real log is
    never written. It proves that:
      • nothing is written, and no folder is created, before a failure;
      • a real caught exception produces one readable record with the
        timestamp+zone, severity, exception type, message, stack, operation,
        module and application version;
      • credentials, long account numbers and e-mail addresses are redacted;
      • a write that cannot happen returns false, throws nothing and leaves the
        reason in LastWriteFailure (logging never becomes the incident);
      • an identical repeat inside the window is counted, not re-written.

    It does NOT prove process-level coverage (a dispatcher crash or a fatal
    AppDomain fault) — those need a real WPF launch, and the audit document says
    so instead of claiming them.

    Run on Windows/.NET 8: open a terminal in this folder and run
      dotnet run
    (This folder holds exactly this one project. The long form of the project
    switch cannot be written here: an XML comment may not contain a double
    hyphen, which is what broke this file before round 34.1.)
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows7.0</TargetFramework>
    <UseWPF>true</UseWPF>
    <EnableWindowsTargeting>true</EnableWindowsTargeting>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <AssemblyName>AppLogBehaviourChecks</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>ProGlassAutomation.Diagnostics.Checks</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../ProGlassAutomation.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
